WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.867 --> 00:00:23.781
When Nello was fifteen years old, he, Jehan, and Patrasche still lived together happily in their little hut.

2
00:00:23.782 --> 00:00:26.651
Life had not changed.

3
00:00:26.652 --> 00:00:30.751
Nello and Patrasche delivered the milk daily.

4
00:00:30.752 --> 00:00:36.637
Nello still dreamed of being an artist and drew pictures every day.

5
00:00:36.638 --> 00:00:42.482
On one fine day, Nello and Patrasche had finished their work.

6
00:00:42.483 --> 00:00:48.103
As usual, they went to find Nello's friend Alois to play.

7
00:00:48.104 --> 00:00:54.716
She was Nello's best friend, and they had played together for many years.

8
00:00:54.717 --> 00:00:57.250
Alois was twelve.

9
00:00:57.251 --> 00:01:00.526
She had no brothers or sisters.

10
00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:05.211
Her father, the miller, was the richest man in the village.

11
00:01:05.212 --> 00:01:08.926
Her little dresses were always pretty.

12
00:01:08.927 --> 00:01:15.833
Her cheeks were rosy, and her sweet, dark eyes shone.

13
00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:21.475
Many families wanted their sons to marry her when she was older.

14
00:01:21.476 --> 00:01:25.875
But Alois had no interest in older boys.

15
00:01:25.876 --> 00:01:32.891
She just loved playing with her friend Nello and his great, friendly dog.

16
00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:40.341
First, Alois, Nello, and Patrasche went up to the old, gray church together.

17
00:01:40.342 --> 00:01:46.822
Then they raced to the fields and played hide-and-seek in the long cornflowers.

18
00:01:46.823 --> 00:01:51.069
Later they lay down, exhausted.

19
00:01:51.070 --> 00:01:57.334
Alois took a little nap, and Patrasche laid his head in her lap.

20
00:01:57.335 --> 00:02:03.540
Nello found a clean piece of pine wood and took out a stick of charcoal.

21
00:02:03.541 --> 00:02:09.259
He started to draw a small portrait of Alois and Patrasche.

22
00:02:09.260 --> 00:02:12.787
Nello drew quickly and confidently.

23
00:02:12.788 --> 00:02:18.189
He drew Alois' dark hair falling on her bright cheeks.

24
00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:23.148
He drew Patrasche's golden fur shining in the sun.

25
00:02:23.149 --> 00:02:28.653
Behind them, a patch of flowers tilted in the breeze.

26
00:02:28.654 --> 00:02:33.591
Alois' father, the miller, came walking into the field.

27
00:02:33.592 --> 00:02:37.962
He was a good man, but was a strict father.

28
00:02:37.963 --> 00:02:42.844
When he saw the portrait, tears came to his eyes.

29
00:02:42.845 --> 00:02:46.752
It captured his daughter's likeness perfectly.

30
00:02:46.753 --> 00:02:50.160
It was beautiful.

31
00:02:50.161 --> 00:02:53.680
The miller told Alois to go home.

32
00:02:53.681 --> 00:02:57.445
"Your mother wants you," he said.

33
00:02:57.446 --> 00:03:02.352
"But Daddy, I'm having fun!" Alois protested.

34
00:03:02.353 --> 00:03:07.488
"Obey your father," the miller said roughly.

35
00:03:07.489 --> 00:03:13.493
The miller snatched the wood from Nello's hands and looked at it closely.

36
00:03:13.494 --> 00:03:18.810
"Do you make drawings of my daughter a lot?" he asked.

37
00:03:18.811 --> 00:03:21.620
His voice trembled.

38
00:03:21.621 --> 00:03:25.029
Nello blushed and hung his head.

39
00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:29.337
"I draw everything I see," he murmured.

40
00:03:29.338 --> 00:03:32.034
The miller was silent.

41
00:03:32.035 --> 00:03:36.679
He thought about Nello and his life of poverty.

42
00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:40.165
Then the miller held out a coin.

43
00:03:40.166 --> 00:03:44.688
"Drawing is a foolish pastime," he said.

44
00:03:44.689 --> 00:03:47.844
"But the picture is like Alois.

45
00:03:47.845 --> 00:03:50.368
It will please her mother.

46
00:03:50.369 --> 00:03:54.663
Take this coin and I will take the picture."

47
00:03:54.664 --> 00:03:57.514
Nello stopped blushing.

48
00:03:57.515 --> 00:04:02.464
He lifted his head and put his hands behind his back.

49
00:04:02.465 --> 00:04:08.107
"Keep the money and keep the portrait, Master Cogez," he said simply.

50
00:04:08.108 --> 00:04:11.716
"You have often been good to me."

51
00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:14.950
Then Nello called Patrasche.

52
00:04:14.951 --> 00:04:18.442
Together they walked home across the field.

53
00:04:18.443 --> 00:04:25.452
"With that coin, I might have seen the master's paintings," he said to Patrasche.

54
00:04:25.453 --> 00:04:34.062
"But I could not sell her picture─not even for them."
